1
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:47,880
Next time, just come here
to make photocopies.

2
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:51,720
Life isn't easy for you.
Don't waste money at the copy shop.

3
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:53,760
Thank you, miss.

4
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:55,040
However,

5
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:58,080
you still have to join group activities

6
00:01:58,160 --> 00:01:59,800
like class meetings and lectures.

7
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:03,480
Just skip what you can
and don't be late if you can help it.

8
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,039
Chen Yanzhou,

9
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:09,960
what happened to you?

10
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:16,320
I was careless.

11
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:19,640
I came to ask about the elective PE class.

12
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:22,480
The football teacher said
he didn't receive my request,

13
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:23,520
but I submitted it.

14
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:29,000
After discussing it
with the Academic Affairs Office,

15
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:30,960
we think football isn't right for you.

16
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:33,760
You had heart problems in the past.

17
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:36,160
What if intense exercise
causes you to have a relapse?

18
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:38,680
I've submitted my physical exam results.

19
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:40,120
I've already recovered.

20
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:43,800
Our university has many other PE courses.

21
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:46,600
Tai chi, yoga, and aerobics

22
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:48,000
are all more moderate.

23
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:49,840
I can approve any of those.

24
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:52,840
Right, Zheng Yu.

25
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:55,040
You chose the tai chi class, right?

26
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:56,080
Isn't it easy?

27
00:02:58,600 --> 00:02:59,440
Rollerblading.

28
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:03,880
I must've remembered wrong.

29
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:06,040
Rollerblading isn't bad either.

30
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:07,560
How is the class?

31
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:11,720
Pretty good. The teacher is kind.

32
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:12,920
Good class vibe too.

33
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
A newbie could pick it up easily.

34
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:16,760
How about rollerblading?

35
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:20,000
Miss, I'll just be frank.

36
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:22,960
I chose football because I'm good at it.

37
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,720
As long as I'm not absent or tardy,

38
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,520
and don't get a substitute,

39
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:29,440
I'll have a guaranteed perfect score.

40
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:31,800
Besides, my choice complies
with the rules.

41
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:34,080
I can't think of any reason
I can't take it.

42
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:38,800
You have to understand

43
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:42,040
that we have to be prudent
as teachers sometimes.

44
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:45,480
Moreover, your family circumstances
are rather unique.

45
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:52,440
How about this?

46
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:54,320
Let's compromise.

47
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:57,360
Fill this out.

48
00:03:57,880 --> 00:03:59,560
Get your doctor to sign off on it.

49
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:03,520
If the doctor confirms that
you can handle the physical load,

50
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:06,120
I will personally submit your application.

51
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:07,400
But I…

52
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:15,680
Thank you, miss.

53
00:04:21,519 --> 00:04:22,440
Zheng Yu,

54
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:26,080
as it happens, I want to talk to you.

55
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:29,560
Your academic performance
in the past two years has been good.

56
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:31,440
Do you have any plans

57
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:34,760
to boost your learning
outside the classroom?

58
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:37,360
Our college has a professor

59
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:41,240
who has a spot for an undergraduate
in her lab this semester.

60
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:44,640
The lab works on real projects
through industry partnerships.

61
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:47,640
As soon as I heard, I thought of you.

62
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:51,200
If you can get in,
it would be a great learning experience.

63
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:55,080
If I get in, do I get to work on
paid projects right away?

64
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:57,200
Not so fast.

65
00:04:57,280 --> 00:05:01,400
You will have to at least get a doctorate
first, or secure funding as a postdoc.

66
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,200
There is plenty of time.
Look ahead to the future.

67
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:06,800
Miss,

68
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,400
only those who have everything

69
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:11,640
can look far ahead like that.

70
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:13,840
For someone like me,

71
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:15,880
what is in front of me

72
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:17,840
is all I can see.

73
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:23,040
What I mean by "look ahead to the future"

74
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:25,160
is your overall plan.

75
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:27,200
Who can succeed instantly?

76
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:31,240
With your GPA, if you get into the lab,

77
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:33,560
you're guaranteed to get
the Vitality Award.

78
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:37,600
- The Vitality Award?
- Yes.

79
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:39,920
Lab research will get you extra points

80
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,880
when applying for the Vitality Award.

81
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:43,760
It's a new regulation this semester.

82
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,560
It counts more than a high GPA.

83
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:49,520
Which professor's lab?

84
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:52,480
Professor Cheng Xiulin.

85
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:54,520
I'll get the document for you.

86
00:05:58,080 --> 00:06:00,000
<i>Lab research will get you extra points</i>

87
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:02,040
<i>when applying for the Vitality Award.</i>

88
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:03,800
<i>It's a new regulation this semester.</i>

89
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:05,440
<i>It counts more than a high GPA.</i>

90
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:17,240
<i>Linjie, I want to ask you</i>

91
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:19,480
<i>about Cheng Xiulin's lab.</i>

92
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:20,840
<i>When is a good time?</i>

93
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:22,200
WANG LINJIE

94
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,320
<i>How about tomorrow? Come see me.</i>

95
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:29,880
PROFESSOR CHENG XIULIN

96
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:33,240
Okay, that's pretty much it.

97
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:36,160
If you have questions,
you can ask me anytime.

98
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:37,480
Thanks, Linjie.

99
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:43,320
Ms. Cheng was just here.

100
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:44,840
I was going to introduce you.

101
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:47,320
Maybe she had to step out.

102
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:49,400
It's okay. Thank you, Linjie.

103
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:50,640
You're welcome.

104
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:54,120
BULLETIN BOARD

105
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:57,920
Professor Cheng.

106
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,640
Have you recovered?

107
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:04,240
I'm fine now.

108
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:06,960
I'm sorry for the trouble.

109
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:08,680
In all my years as a teacher,

110
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:11,040
you're the first student of mine
to collapse in the lab.

111
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:16,560
I haven't had the chance
to apologize to you in person.

112
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:18,680
Chen Yanzhou,

113
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:21,160
I'm not the one you should apologize to.

114
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:23,240
It's yourself.

115
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:24,840
And your parents.

116
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:28,040
If something truly had happened that day…

117
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:31,640
Do you intend
to put them through that again?

118
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:35,680
Do I still have a chance to come back?

119
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:41,560
I will email the application.

120
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:44,720
I hope you can view each resume fairly.

121
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:47,440
I'm busy. I have to go.

122
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:15,520
Looks like Cheng Xiulin didn't agree
to let you return.

123
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,080
UNDERGRADUATE RECRUITMENT NOTICE

124
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:21,680
No, she didn't.

125
00:08:22,400 --> 00:08:25,880
So I'll have to compete
for the sole undergraduate spot.

126
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,680
You're more impressive than I thought.

127
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:33,840
You spare no effort
for the Vitality Award.

128
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:36,520
You're no better.

129
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:40,039
To boost your GPA,
you won't even change your PE class,

130
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:41,360
disregarding your health.

131
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:47,080
We're not close enough
to care about each other's health.

132
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:52,360
Instead of trying to cozy up to me,
why not compete properly?

133
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:54,280
Fine.

134
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,840
<i>Don't you dare be late today.</i>

135
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,000
LU SIQUAN (STORE MANAGER)

136
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:15,280
Do you know why indoor cats
can never beat stray cats?

137
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:21,320
Because indoor cats fight as play.

138
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:24,520
Stray cats fight

139
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,600
for survival.

140
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:36,840
UNDERGRADUATE APPLICATION
FOR CHENG XIULIN'S LABORATORY

141
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:44,080
<i>Zheng Yu, here's the latest news.</i>

142
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:47,000
<i>Does your class have a new student</i>
<i>named Chen Yanzhou?</i>

143
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:50,360
<i>I heard he also applied</i>
<i>for the spot in Ms. Cheng's lab.</i>

144
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:52,200
<i>He's a strong competitor.</i>

145
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:53,440
WANG LINJIE

146
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:55,320
<i>You might not know.</i>

147
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:57,560
<i>He used to do research with Ms. Cheng.</i>

148
00:09:57,640 --> 00:10:00,920
<i>He only withdrew due to medical reasons.</i>

149
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:05,440
<i>I know.</i>

150
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:06,920
CERTIFICATE OF RECOVERY

151
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,760
I really can't sign this.

152
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:12,840
I have no way to confirm or supervise
the intensity of this class.

153
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:15,520
What if I sign this and something happens?

154
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:16,960
I know I can do it.

155
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:20,040
You're confident, but I'm not.

156
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:21,640
How about this?

157
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:24,800
I'll give you a medical exemption note
to give to your teacher.

158
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:27,600
An exemption only gives me a pass.

159
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:29,040
I want the credit.

160
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:32,520
Your university's PE courses
aren't that important.

161
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:34,360
You're so strange.

162
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:37,280
So many students ask me for an exemption

163
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:38,880
so they can slack off.

164
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:41,600
You, on the contrary, want the trouble.

165
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:45,600
That's all the more reason
that I can't sign this.

166
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,200
Hello?

167
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:54,200
<i>Hello.</i>

168
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:56,880
<i>This is the Shang'an Road Police Station.</i>

169
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:58,760
<i>Are you Mr. Chen Yanzhou?</i>

170
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:04,640
Look. Do you see that?

171
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:07,520
This was when your wallet was stolen.

172
00:11:08,280 --> 00:11:10,760
If this thief hadn't
committed another crime there,

173
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:12,240
we wouldn't have found this.

174
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:18,400
Do you know this girl?

175
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:23,280
What about her?

176
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:24,760
The thief said

177
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:26,240
this girl followed him

178
00:11:26,320 --> 00:11:28,840
to the emergency staircase
and got the wallet back.

179
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:34,720
<i>There happened to be no CCTV there.</i>

180
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:37,200
<i>We didn't know</i>
<i>if he was telling the truth,</i>

181
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:41,200
<i>so we asked you to come mainly to check</i>
<i>if that girl returned the wallet to you.</i>

182
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:50,440
ZY, ADD TO ADDRESS BOOK

183
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:55,080
SEND FRIEND REQUEST

184
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:00,520
I'M CYZ
IN THE "LIFE SCIENCES CLASS 1" GROUP

185
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:02,120
<i>On campus?</i>

186
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:05,360
ZHENG YU

187
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:08,240
FAST NEIGHBOR (THE QING YI UNIVERSITY
OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY BRANCH)

188
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:30,400
<i>Six hours have passed.</i>

189
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:32,400
<i>We now change the cell culture medium.</i>

190
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:33,440
<i>Take out our cells…</i>

191
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:40,600
Did you install this wind chime?

192
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:43,600
That's smart.

193
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:45,360
What do you want?

194
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:48,880
Why didn't you say

195
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:52,000
you got the wallet back from the thief?

196
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:54,600
You weren't wrong that day.

197
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:56,880
Even if you hadn't made that post,

198
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:58,920
I would still have asked you for money.

199
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:03,360
If I were a kind, selfless,
and good person seeking no reward,

200
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:05,880
when he made his move in the elevator,

201
00:13:06,560 --> 00:13:08,240
I would have called him out on it.

202
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:10,440
But I'm not.

203
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:15,320
So what does it matter
whether I said it or not?

204
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:18,080
At least I would think--

205
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:20,720
At least I would seem less detestable?

206
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:23,760
I don't care what others think.

207
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,760
I already got what I wanted.

208
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:33,680
Also,

209
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:35,320
we're not so close

210
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:37,120
as to sit and chat.

211
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:40,640
In your own words,
instead of trying to cozy up to me…

212
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:44,360
why not compete properly?

213
00:13:58,520 --> 00:14:00,080
<i>Hello, Professor Cheng Xiulin.</i>

214
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:03,320
<i>I'm Chen Yanzhou, a Life Sciences junior.</i>

215
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:07,800
<i>I hope to have the chance</i>
<i>to join your lab.</i>

216
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:20,400
SELLING PERFUME (MINOR FLAW)
ON RQ SECONDHAND GOODS

217
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:38,320
MOLECULAR MECHANISM
BY WHICH THE CXN48 GENE…

218
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:46,280
Zheng Yu,

219
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:49,560
can you dim the light a bit?

220
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:51,800
The brightness is keeping me awake.

221
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:15,120
Did you send the email?

222
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:17,040
Yes.

223
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:18,320
What did Ms. Cheng say?

224
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:23,800
Actually, don't pin
all your hopes on that.

225
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:26,920
You can try different things.

226
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,800
You could try a different research topic.

227
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:39,480
What about your choice of PE class?

228
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:41,800
The university and the hospital

229
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:43,600
won't let me take football.

230
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:45,400
What did you pick then?

231
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:49,880
This is a new addition to our class.
Chen Yanzhou.

232
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:52,720
By the way, which college are you in?

233
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:54,440
Life Sciences.

234
00:15:55,560 --> 00:15:57,080
That's the same as Zheng Yu.

235
00:15:57,680 --> 00:15:59,200
Different majors, though.

236
00:16:00,040 --> 00:16:01,640
- Same class.
- Okay.

237
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:02,800
In that case,

238
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:05,040
Zheng Yu, you can look after him.

239
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:07,800
Everyone else, listen up.

240
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:10,800
During practice, help each other out.

241
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:12,720
Then you will improve faster. Got it?

242
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:14,440
- Got it.
- Got it.

243
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:16,440
Wait.

244
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:18,760
Where are your rollerblades?

245
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:24,280
Borrow a pair from the equipment room!

246
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:25,760
When you show up,

247
00:16:25,840 --> 00:16:28,920
either bring your own pair
or borrow a pair in advance.

248
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,560
Don't be unprepared again. Got it?

249
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:35,920
<i>The teacher is kind. Good class vibe too.</i>

250
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:44,720
I suggest you get a medical exemption.

251
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:46,520
You can still get a pass.

252
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:49,840
And you? So what if you can rollerblade?

253
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:52,040
Has Cheng Xiulin replied to you?

254
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:55,240
I heard you don't have any lab experience.

255
00:16:55,320 --> 00:16:57,680
Getting the spot will be hard.

256
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:05,880
<i>A newbie could pick it up easily.</i>

257
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:07,200
Why pick this class?

258
00:17:11,520 --> 00:17:12,720
I didn't pick it.

259
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:13,960
Someone paid to swap.

260
00:17:17,079 --> 00:17:18,520
At your skill level,

261
00:17:18,599 --> 00:17:19,720
how can you teach me?

262
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:06,320
I'll say this first.

263
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:08,000
If you cut class,

264
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:09,920
I won't cover for you.

265
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:12,520
I just need the restroom.

266
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:32,080
I should've known.

267
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:39,160
CAMPUS LEARNING WEEK: ENCOUNTER
A BETTER VERSION OF YOURSELF.

268
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:52,920
You can definitely beat him.

269
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:56,720
- What?
- I was in the equipment room.

270
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:58,640
Chen Yanzhou was borrowing rollerblades.

271
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,080
He can't do it at all.

272
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,840
You can definitely win.

273
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:04,480
I don't care about winning.

274
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:16,680
<i>I never tell myself that I want to win.</i>

275
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:18,760
<i>My only thought is that I must not lose.</i>

276
00:19:20,600 --> 00:19:22,920
<i>The desire to win stems from expectations.</i>

277
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,360
<i>The desire not to lose</i>

278
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:26,000
<i>is because there is no way out.</i>

279
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:29,760
<i>With this mindset,</i>

280
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:32,480
<i>I hurry across campus</i>
<i>in the early morning.</i>

281
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:54,440
<i>I'm not the only one in a hurry.</i>

282
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:23,560
It's scary.

283
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:26,120
- What?
- I was reading comics at the library.

284
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:28,120
Zheng Yu and Chen Yanzhou

285
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:30,720
studied there all afternoon
and never got up.

286
00:20:32,920 --> 00:20:35,960
I heard they're competing
to get into Ms. Cheng's lab.

287
00:20:36,040 --> 00:20:37,960
Zheng Yu is our roommate,

288
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:41,120
but I think Cheng Xiulin will choose
Chen Yanzhou.

289
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:42,240
He was there first.

290
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:44,560
Not necessarily.

291
00:20:45,920 --> 00:20:48,920
Maybe Zheng Yu will impress her more.

292
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:03,560
<i>Zheng Yu, your application</i>
<i>form has been received.</i>

293
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:05,560
<i>The written test, interview time,</i>

294
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:07,120
<i>location, and notes</i>

295
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,720
<i>have been sent to you.</i>

296
00:21:08,800 --> 00:21:10,360
<i>Please check your inbox.</i>

297
00:21:14,160 --> 00:21:15,560
<i>Chen Yanzhou,</i>

298
00:21:15,640 --> 00:21:17,480
<i>your application form has been received.</i>

299
00:21:17,560 --> 00:21:20,880
<i>The written test, interview time,</i>
<i>location, and notes</i>

300
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:22,160
<i>have been sent to you.</i>

301
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:23,880
<i>Please check your inbox.</i>

302
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:25,600
<i>Cheng Xiulin's laboratory.</i>

303
00:21:47,040 --> 00:21:49,600
Today's written test doesn't
seem too hard.

304
00:22:31,400 --> 00:22:33,040
Next, Zheng Yu.

305
00:22:41,520 --> 00:22:43,080
ZHENG YU, COLLEGE OF LIFE SCIENCES

306
00:22:43,160 --> 00:22:44,320
Zheng Yu.

307
00:22:46,120 --> 00:22:49,080
The resume you submitted
left a deep impression.

308
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:53,000
It seems you did a lot of research
when writing your application.

309
00:22:53,600 --> 00:22:54,440
However,

310
00:22:54,520 --> 00:22:56,400
I'm not looking
to recruit an undergraduate

311
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:58,800
to do simple data organization,

312
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:01,960
assist their upperclassmen,

313
00:23:02,040 --> 00:23:03,400
and be free labor.

314
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:07,320
I hope that they can truly be
involved in the project

315
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:11,120
and find a role that suits them
in the project.

316
00:23:12,080 --> 00:23:12,920
Of course.

317
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:16,920
If it were only for the former,
I wouldn't be here.

318
00:23:18,360 --> 00:23:22,000
I see you were recommended for admission
after a biology competition.

319
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:25,360
That shows you have great potential.

320
00:23:25,440 --> 00:23:27,040
And in the past two years,

321
00:23:27,120 --> 00:23:29,880
your grades in your major
have been excellent.

322
00:23:30,880 --> 00:23:33,160
Honestly, I'm quite satisfied with you.

323
00:23:34,280 --> 00:23:37,840
However, you haven't applied
to any labs before.

324
00:23:38,560 --> 00:23:40,360
What consideration lies behind this?

325
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:43,640
I…

326
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:50,880
I don't want to lie.

327
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:54,440
Due to personal reasons,
I need to make money.

328
00:23:55,080 --> 00:23:56,840
So for the past two years,

329
00:23:57,800 --> 00:23:59,320
I've been busy working.

330
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:02,640
What are your plans for the future?

331
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:19,840
Next, Chen Yanzhou.

332
00:24:22,360 --> 00:24:23,400
<i>Originally,</i>

333
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:26,240
I wasn't inclined
to approve your application.

334
00:24:26,320 --> 00:24:27,520
But you were right.

335
00:24:28,120 --> 00:24:30,120
I should judge fairly.

336
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:32,200
Your grades and experience

337
00:24:32,280 --> 00:24:34,920
are sufficient to take you to this stage.

338
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:39,280
I hope you can give me a chance
to start over again.

339
00:24:58,880 --> 00:25:01,840
Do you know
what truly starting over means?

340
00:26:10,160 --> 00:26:11,040
Buying something?

341
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:19,560
Ring me up.

342
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:24,400
That's 4,260 yuan.

343
00:26:35,520 --> 00:26:37,720
I'll pay the rest with WeChat Pay.

344
00:26:42,240 --> 00:26:43,160
Finished?

345
00:26:43,240 --> 00:26:44,080
Thank you.

346
00:26:44,160 --> 00:26:45,000
You're welcome.

347
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:50,960
Whose beautiful daughter is this?

348
00:26:52,240 --> 00:26:54,760
Ms. Yang, sorry for troubling you
during this time.

349
00:26:54,840 --> 00:26:56,240
Why are you being so polite?

350
00:26:57,200 --> 00:26:58,960
You seem to have lost weight again.

351
00:26:59,040 --> 00:27:01,600
Have you been eating and resting properly?

352
00:27:02,760 --> 00:27:03,920
You clearly haven't.

353
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:08,320
Say, you finally paid off
the hospital charges.

354
00:27:08,400 --> 00:27:10,720
Then you come here,
and you're on your laptop.

355
00:27:12,240 --> 00:27:13,360
Xiaozheng,

356
00:27:13,440 --> 00:27:16,120
sometimes, you need to catch your breath.

357
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:19,080
All the part-time gigs

358
00:27:19,160 --> 00:27:22,120
were originally enough to pay
for hospitalization costs.

359
00:27:22,200 --> 00:27:28,000
But now, I don't know
when a costly emergency might come up.

360
00:27:28,640 --> 00:27:31,760
And on top of that, at the end
of each semester, I have to…

361
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:34,400
You have to what?

362
00:27:36,840 --> 00:27:38,120
Nothing.

363
00:27:38,200 --> 00:27:41,680
I'm just wondering if I can get
the Vitality Award this semester.

364
00:27:43,200 --> 00:27:46,120
You said before that
only your college offers it.

365
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:47,040
Right?

366
00:27:48,560 --> 00:27:50,240
I'm wondering,

367
00:27:50,320 --> 00:27:52,320
how come only your college has it?

368
00:27:52,920 --> 00:27:58,000
The city's top scholar six years ago
could have gone to a better institution.

369
00:27:58,080 --> 00:28:01,000
But he chose to go to Qing Yi University's
College of Life Sciences

370
00:28:01,080 --> 00:28:02,200
to study thale cress.

371
00:28:02,280 --> 00:28:04,000
Thale what?

372
00:28:05,880 --> 00:28:08,440
It's a weed that grows by the roadside.

373
00:28:09,040 --> 00:28:10,760
How is a weed worth researching?

374
00:28:11,520 --> 00:28:14,320
Geniuses always
know their calling early on.

375
00:28:14,920 --> 00:28:18,280
Some companies wanted to sponsor him
and set up a fund

376
00:28:18,360 --> 00:28:20,400
to encourage people like him.

377
00:28:21,120 --> 00:28:23,200
It's what is now the Vitality Award.

378
00:28:23,280 --> 00:28:24,360
I remember.

379
00:28:24,440 --> 00:28:26,520
You previously said

380
00:28:26,600 --> 00:28:28,760
that this award was the reason

381
00:28:29,520 --> 00:28:30,760
you didn't change majors.

382
00:28:32,160 --> 00:28:33,000
It pays a lot.

383
00:28:33,600 --> 00:28:36,440
Then this top scholar

384
00:28:36,520 --> 00:28:38,760
is a guide in your academic journey.

385
00:28:39,880 --> 00:28:41,760
What is he doing now?

386
00:28:41,840 --> 00:28:43,160
He's so incredible.

387
00:28:43,240 --> 00:28:45,200
By now, he must have a PhD.

388
00:28:45,280 --> 00:28:46,120
A teacher?

389
00:28:46,200 --> 00:28:48,760
Maybe he even became his own boss.

390
00:28:49,600 --> 00:28:50,440
I don't know.

391
00:28:51,080 --> 00:28:53,320
I don't even have enough time for myself,

392
00:28:53,400 --> 00:28:55,440
much less to wonder about other people.

393
00:28:56,800 --> 00:28:58,200
Don't say that.

394
00:28:58,280 --> 00:29:00,680
Regardless of what job you do
in the future,

395
00:29:01,720 --> 00:29:04,440
nothing bad can come from knowing more.

396
00:29:05,680 --> 00:29:06,800
Maybe

397
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:08,600
it can give you more options.

398
00:29:31,560 --> 00:29:33,800
WHO IS ZHOU GUANQI, QINGYI'S TOP SCHOLAR?

399
00:29:33,880 --> 00:29:36,720
ZHOU GUANQI
WINS NATIONAL BIOLOGY COMPETITION

400
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:46,880
<i>Does anyone know what Qingyi's top scholar</i>
<i>six years ago, Zhou Guanqi, is doing now?</i>

401
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:50,560
POST

402
00:29:53,880 --> 00:29:57,520
DOES ANYONE KNOW WHAT QINGYI'S TOP SCHOLAR
SIX YEARS AGO, ZHOU GUANQI, IS DOING NOW?

403
00:30:18,960 --> 00:30:19,880
We're closing.

404
00:30:20,960 --> 00:30:22,880
Are you going to eat those noodles?

405
00:30:28,840 --> 00:30:29,680
No.

406
00:30:33,040 --> 00:30:33,920
I'll take them home.

407
00:30:40,720 --> 00:30:42,240
What a weirdo.

408
00:30:49,040 --> 00:30:51,720
Xiaozheng, are you not returning
to your dorm tonight?

409
00:30:52,600 --> 00:30:53,720
I'll sleep here today.

410
00:30:54,600 --> 00:30:55,960
Don't sleep hunched over.

411
00:30:56,040 --> 00:30:57,720
It's bad for your spine.

412
00:30:57,800 --> 00:30:58,640
Use this.

413
00:30:59,280 --> 00:31:00,880
It's getting colder now.

414
00:31:01,560 --> 00:31:04,840
There is a blanket
in the bag next to my mom's bed.

415
00:31:04,920 --> 00:31:06,560
Don't mind it. It's clean.

416
00:31:06,640 --> 00:31:08,400
I just washed it a few days ago.

417
00:31:09,080 --> 00:31:10,240
Thank you.

418
00:31:10,920 --> 00:31:12,160
I'm leaving.

419
00:31:12,840 --> 00:31:15,720
When the caregiver isn't here,
please look after her.

420
00:31:15,800 --> 00:31:17,040
Thank you.

421
00:31:42,800 --> 00:31:44,280
<i>Hello, Zheng Yu.</i>

422
00:31:44,360 --> 00:31:46,520
<i>Thank you for your trust</i>

423
00:31:46,600 --> 00:31:49,920
<i>and the effort you put into</i>
<i>the written test and interview,</i>

424
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:53,760
<i>but we have found a suitable candidate</i>
<i>for the undergraduate position.</i>

425
00:31:53,840 --> 00:31:57,240
<i>You're welcome</i>
<i>to visit the laboratory and learn.</i>

426
00:32:57,640 --> 00:32:59,320
Others rise to the rooster's crow.

427
00:32:59,400 --> 00:33:02,000
You probably get up
earlier than the rooster.

428
00:33:02,920 --> 00:33:04,360
The early bird gets the worm.

429
00:33:06,560 --> 00:33:07,400
Got it.

430
00:33:07,480 --> 00:33:10,520
You got the worm, and now
you're showing off. Congratulations.

431
00:33:15,080 --> 00:33:17,720
Didn't you receive an email from the lab?

432
00:33:17,800 --> 00:33:18,640
I did.

433
00:33:18,720 --> 00:33:20,520
Then why are you congratulating me?

434
00:33:20,600 --> 00:33:21,600
I didn't get in.

435
00:33:25,560 --> 00:33:26,520
What a coincidence.

436
00:33:27,120 --> 00:33:27,960
I didn't either.

437
00:33:39,960 --> 00:33:42,160
<i>Human emotions are</i>
<i>as fickle as the weather.</i>

438
00:33:43,200 --> 00:33:45,920
<i>I thought only successful people</i>
<i>share their joy.</i>

439
00:33:48,800 --> 00:33:50,560
<i>Turns out two failures</i>

440
00:33:50,640 --> 00:33:52,720
<i>don't need to say a word</i>

441
00:33:52,800 --> 00:33:55,160
<i>to feel an inexplicable closeness.</i>

442
00:34:03,080 --> 00:34:06,640
Ms. Cheng choosing Zhang Rui
is understandable.

443
00:34:06,720 --> 00:34:07,960
You don't know, do you?

444
00:34:08,040 --> 00:34:10,520
Zhang Rui has been guaranteed admission
into our graduate program

445
00:34:10,600 --> 00:34:12,880
and will keep working in the lab
as a graduate student.

446
00:34:12,960 --> 00:34:14,679
It meets the hiring standards.

447
00:34:14,760 --> 00:34:15,600
So

448
00:34:16,159 --> 00:34:17,520
don't let it get to you.

449
00:34:20,080 --> 00:34:21,199
Are you listening?

450
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:24,159
I understand.

451
00:34:24,239 --> 00:34:27,080
No matter who got in,
it doesn't affect me.

452
00:34:27,159 --> 00:34:28,679
Besides,

453
00:34:28,760 --> 00:34:30,520
I'm not the only one who failed.

454
00:34:30,600 --> 00:34:33,440
If I were too fragile to take it,
wouldn't I seem useless?

455
00:34:39,639 --> 00:34:40,480
What?

456
00:34:40,560 --> 00:34:42,800
I thought you would be depressed
for a while.

457
00:34:44,239 --> 00:34:45,600
I don't have time for that.

458
00:34:46,480 --> 00:34:49,679
You've been on your phone
since you got here. What is it?

459
00:34:49,760 --> 00:34:52,239
My advisor wants to talk
about the Sports Meet.

460
00:34:53,719 --> 00:34:55,320
You were banned from PE classes.

461
00:34:55,400 --> 00:34:57,480
What can you do with the Sports Meet?

462
00:34:58,320 --> 00:35:00,840
I don't have enough
community service credits.

463
00:35:00,920 --> 00:35:03,200
She wants me to volunteer
at the Sports Meet.

464
00:35:03,280 --> 00:35:04,440
Then go.

465
00:35:05,640 --> 00:35:07,720
I was going to wait until the winter break

466
00:35:07,800 --> 00:35:10,160
and do volunteer work
in the community with my mom.

467
00:35:10,240 --> 00:35:12,560
She gives environmental science talks.

468
00:35:12,640 --> 00:35:15,240
Getting proof of volunteer service
would be easy.

469
00:35:16,680 --> 00:35:19,760
I think getting it done early
at the university would be better.

470
00:35:20,800 --> 00:35:22,760
Your advisor has it tough.

471
00:35:22,840 --> 00:35:26,080
Juniors and seniors
hardly ever participate at the meet.

472
00:35:26,160 --> 00:35:28,800
We get it. Seniors have
one foot out the door.

473
00:35:28,880 --> 00:35:31,320
But many junior classes
have zero participation.

474
00:35:31,400 --> 00:35:34,120
The numbers look terrible
when they're reported.

475
00:35:34,200 --> 00:35:37,120
I heard the college
wants to boost participation

476
00:35:37,200 --> 00:35:38,880
and even set up monetary prizes.

477
00:35:39,480 --> 00:35:41,640
The prize for a gold medal
is only 500 yuan.

478
00:35:41,720 --> 00:35:43,280
I don't think it will help.

479
00:35:43,360 --> 00:35:45,320
THE 26TH SPORTS MEET REGISTRATION

480
00:35:47,240 --> 00:35:50,040
It's just the Sports Meet.
All categories are full.

481
00:35:50,800 --> 00:35:52,600
Sign up for something unpopular.

482
00:35:52,680 --> 00:35:55,880
Fewer competitors means
a higher chance of winning a medal.

483
00:35:56,600 --> 00:35:57,440
You don't say.

484
00:35:57,520 --> 00:36:00,640
They told me to sign up
for a long-distance race.

485
00:36:00,720 --> 00:36:02,760
Class 1 has signed up, but not our class.

486
00:36:02,840 --> 00:36:04,680
Who is so brave in Class 1?

487
00:36:04,760 --> 00:36:06,600
No idea. Let me see.

488
00:36:06,680 --> 00:36:08,280
800 M, 1500 M, 3000 M, 100 M

489
00:36:10,360 --> 00:36:11,600
ZHENG YU

490
00:36:11,680 --> 00:36:12,880
Zheng Yu.

491
00:36:13,600 --> 00:36:15,000
Zheng Yu?

492
00:36:15,080 --> 00:36:17,200
I thought she wouldn't participate.

493
00:36:17,280 --> 00:36:19,960
This… This personal shopper can't
be trusted.

494
00:36:20,880 --> 00:36:23,040
This size 37 feels like a size 36.

495
00:36:34,720 --> 00:36:36,280
Major discovery!

496
00:36:36,360 --> 00:36:38,240
Participant information is shown here.

497
00:36:39,400 --> 00:36:40,440
Her birthday is soon.

498
00:36:41,120 --> 00:36:41,960
When is it?

499
00:36:43,760 --> 00:36:45,840
My goodness, Zhuang Ning.
So you were here.

500
00:36:47,720 --> 00:36:48,800
So when is it?

501
00:36:49,880 --> 00:36:51,520
- Friday.
- Friday?

502
00:36:52,240 --> 00:36:53,960
That's the day of the Sports Meet.

503
00:36:59,880 --> 00:37:03,000
1500 M: ZHENG YU, 3000 M: ZHENG YU

504
00:37:05,240 --> 00:37:07,240
Dear teachers and students,

505
00:37:07,320 --> 00:37:08,840
for this crisp autumn season,

506
00:37:08,920 --> 00:37:13,360
we welcome Qing Yi University's 26th
Track and Field Sports Meet.

507
00:37:13,960 --> 00:37:16,760
Let's welcome every participant's
outstanding performance

508
00:37:16,840 --> 00:37:19,760
with great enthusiasm and high spirits.

509
00:37:20,600 --> 00:37:21,520
Thanks.

510
00:37:44,280 --> 00:37:45,760
Sir. Some water.

511
00:37:45,840 --> 00:37:46,680
Thank you.

512
00:37:56,960 --> 00:37:58,680
Wait!

513
00:37:59,720 --> 00:38:00,920
Wait!

514
00:38:02,560 --> 00:38:04,840
Chen Yanzhou from Class 1, right?

515
00:38:04,920 --> 00:38:06,360
Can I have a bottle of water?

516
00:38:07,560 --> 00:38:09,000
These are for the referees.

517
00:38:09,080 --> 00:38:10,520
There's a vending machine over there.

518
00:38:15,600 --> 00:38:16,520
Drink up.

519
00:38:17,320 --> 00:38:20,040
Linlin, you're still the best.

520
00:38:23,320 --> 00:38:26,240
Do you think Zheng Yu
has returned to the dorm yet?

521
00:38:43,960 --> 00:38:45,520
HAPPY BIRTHDAY, ZHENG YU!

522
00:38:49,720 --> 00:38:52,800
<i>Sorry for taking up your desk before.</i>

523
00:38:52,880 --> 00:38:56,560
<i>We can go to class together from now on.</i>
<i>I'll save you a seat.</i>

524
00:38:56,640 --> 00:38:58,680
<i>Happy birthday, Zheng Yu!</i>

525
00:39:22,240 --> 00:39:24,600
Why am I wasting time here?

526
00:39:26,360 --> 00:39:28,360
No way! You're volunteering too!

527
00:39:28,960 --> 00:39:30,200
You are…?

528
00:39:30,280 --> 00:39:33,160
Class 1's class monitor, Zhang Qi.
We're in the same class.

529
00:39:36,840 --> 00:39:38,120
Yan… Yanzhou,

530
00:39:38,200 --> 00:39:39,680
I have to ask you for a favor.

531
00:39:40,680 --> 00:39:42,520
Look, I just got the news.

532
00:39:42,600 --> 00:39:45,960
This afternoon's shot put event
was suddenly moved to tomorrow.

533
00:39:46,040 --> 00:39:46,920
Wrong person.

534
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:48,800
I didn't sign up, and I can't do it.

535
00:39:48,880 --> 00:39:51,080
No, that's not it. I signed up.

536
00:39:51,160 --> 00:39:54,680
But the timing of the event
clashes with my volunteer slot tomorrow.

537
00:39:54,760 --> 00:39:58,400
So I want to ask if you're free tomorrow.

538
00:39:58,480 --> 00:39:59,880
Can you volunteer for me?

539
00:39:59,960 --> 00:40:01,560
It won't take more than an hour.

540
00:40:01,640 --> 00:40:03,280
I'll come as soon as I'm done.

541
00:40:03,360 --> 00:40:06,000
I'm not free. I don't plan
to come to campus tomorrow.

542
00:40:08,280 --> 00:40:09,280
Please help me out.

543
00:40:09,360 --> 00:40:12,560
If I could find anyone else,
I wouldn't trouble you.

544
00:40:12,640 --> 00:40:15,120
Our class's participants
have scheduling conflicts.

545
00:40:15,200 --> 00:40:17,440
For example,
Liu Chen is shot-putting with me.

546
00:40:17,520 --> 00:40:19,000
Xing Mingtao will shoot hoops.

547
00:40:19,080 --> 00:40:21,560
Zheng Yu has the 3000 m race. I really…

548
00:40:22,160 --> 00:40:23,160
Zheng Yu

549
00:40:23,240 --> 00:40:24,640
is running the 3000 m?

550
00:40:27,440 --> 00:40:30,120
What event did you want me
to volunteer for?

551
00:40:30,200 --> 00:40:31,560
The 3000 m race.

552
00:40:33,000 --> 00:40:35,000
Zhang Qi, what were you asking me?

553
00:40:35,080 --> 00:40:36,200
What?

554
00:40:38,960 --> 00:40:42,240
Are you free tomorrow to volunteer for me?

555
00:40:42,840 --> 00:40:44,000
Sure.

556
00:40:50,320 --> 00:40:52,480
You didn't see the hurdler.

557
00:40:52,560 --> 00:40:54,040
Every hurdle fell over.

558
00:40:54,120 --> 00:40:55,520
Be careful.

559
00:40:55,600 --> 00:40:56,680
What if we ruin it?

560
00:40:56,760 --> 00:40:58,480
How will you give it to Zheng Yu?

561
00:40:58,560 --> 00:41:00,640
If I ruin it, I'll buy ten for her.

562
00:41:03,120 --> 00:41:04,480
- Hide it.
- Hide it.

563
00:41:04,560 --> 00:41:05,560
Come on.

564
00:41:05,640 --> 00:41:06,920
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

565
00:41:10,600 --> 00:41:11,440
Let's go.

566
00:41:13,240 --> 00:41:14,360
Quietly.

567
00:41:31,480 --> 00:41:32,520
Still eating cake?

568
00:41:32,600 --> 00:41:33,720
Yes.

569
00:41:33,800 --> 00:41:35,680
I bought it. Why wouldn't we eat it?

570
00:41:43,080 --> 00:41:44,360
It's fine. Sit.

571
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:47,560
Who says we can eat cake
only for a birthday?

572
00:41:47,640 --> 00:41:49,600
We can eat it even without a birthday.

573
00:41:54,200 --> 00:41:55,120
Let's share it.

574
00:42:28,840 --> 00:42:30,960
Are you running the 3000 m
in those shoes?

575
00:42:35,680 --> 00:42:36,640
Why not?

576
00:42:38,920 --> 00:42:40,920
You will be behind at the starting line.

577
00:42:42,520 --> 00:42:43,760
Thanks for the warning.

578
00:42:43,840 --> 00:42:47,720
As it happens, I've never stood
at the same starting line anyway.

579
00:42:56,320 --> 00:42:58,040
Next, we have

580
00:42:58,120 --> 00:43:00,800
the women's 3000 m race,
junior year group.

581
00:43:00,880 --> 00:43:04,000
The juniors only have one group,
eight people in total.

582
00:43:04,080 --> 00:43:07,880
After the race starts,
volunteers will help count your laps.

583
00:43:07,960 --> 00:43:09,520
The finish line is over there.

584
00:43:10,080 --> 00:43:11,000
Later,

585
00:43:11,080 --> 00:43:12,760
I will wait for you there.

586
00:43:16,120 --> 00:43:17,440
JUNIOR WOMEN'S 3000 M LAP COUNT

587
00:43:19,320 --> 00:43:20,840
No. 331 crossed the line.

588
00:43:21,400 --> 00:43:23,280
Okay, make sure not to cross the line.

589
00:43:27,480 --> 00:43:28,720
On your marks.

590
00:43:35,320 --> 00:43:36,480
- Go!
- Go!

591
00:43:36,560 --> 00:43:38,000
We can now see

592
00:43:38,080 --> 00:43:41,000
the junior women's 3000 m race
has officially begun.

593
00:43:41,080 --> 00:43:42,520
Currently in the lead

594
00:43:42,600 --> 00:43:43,960
is No. 331, Tong Ruyi,

595
00:43:44,040 --> 00:43:47,040
from the College of Management.

596
00:43:47,120 --> 00:43:47,960
- Go!
- Go!

597
00:43:48,880 --> 00:43:50,000
- Go!
- Go!

598
00:43:50,080 --> 00:43:51,760
First time volunteering at a meet?

599
00:43:52,280 --> 00:43:53,480
Relax.

600
00:43:53,560 --> 00:43:55,560
The outcome is obvious at a glance.

601
00:43:56,320 --> 00:43:57,440
Why?

602
00:43:57,520 --> 00:44:00,560
No. 323, Li Zheng, was on the track team
as a freshman.

603
00:44:00,640 --> 00:44:02,880
Her movement and form are pro-level.

604
00:44:02,960 --> 00:44:04,240
She's pacing herself.

605
00:44:04,320 --> 00:44:05,400
She will surely win.

606
00:44:07,880 --> 00:44:09,680
Aren't athletes ranked separately?

607
00:44:09,760 --> 00:44:11,440
She left the team last year.

608
00:44:11,520 --> 00:44:13,840
She's good, but not
considered a sports major.

609
00:44:17,520 --> 00:44:19,280
- Go!
- Go!

610
00:44:19,360 --> 00:44:21,840
- Go!
- Go!

611
00:44:21,920 --> 00:44:23,600
- Go!
- Go!

612
00:44:23,680 --> 00:44:24,720
In the second lap,

613
00:44:24,800 --> 00:44:27,800
the eight contestants have separated
into three groups.

614
00:44:27,880 --> 00:44:29,120
We can see

615
00:44:29,200 --> 00:44:32,720
the first group is No. 331 and No. 372.

616
00:44:33,440 --> 00:44:37,360
The second group has No. 323 and No. 308.

617
00:44:37,440 --> 00:44:40,560
Lagging behind
in the third group are No. 357,

618
00:44:40,640 --> 00:44:41,920
No. 339,

619
00:44:42,000 --> 00:44:43,120
No. 351,

620
00:44:43,200 --> 00:44:45,280
and No. 395.

621
00:44:45,360 --> 00:44:47,480
ZHENG YU

622
00:45:06,720 --> 00:45:07,720
LI ZHENG

623
00:45:07,800 --> 00:45:08,640
ZHENG YU

624
00:45:10,560 --> 00:45:11,760
LI ZHENG

625
00:45:14,320 --> 00:45:18,120
The junior women's 3000 m race
has entered the final stage.

626
00:45:18,200 --> 00:45:20,560
No. 323 and No. 308

627
00:45:20,640 --> 00:45:22,680
are the first to enter their sixth lap.

628
00:45:23,280 --> 00:45:26,120
Interestingly,
since the start of the race,

629
00:45:26,200 --> 00:45:27,800
the two contestants

630
00:45:27,880 --> 00:45:29,760
have maintained their positions.

631
00:45:29,840 --> 00:45:33,400
Choosing the right pacer
is very important.

632
00:45:33,480 --> 00:45:37,520
No. 308 has stuck to No. 323's heels.

633
00:45:37,600 --> 00:45:40,560
I have to say it was a very wise decision.

634
00:45:44,040 --> 00:45:46,880
- Go!
- Go!

635
00:45:46,960 --> 00:45:49,440
No. 323 is finally starting to sprint.

636
00:45:49,520 --> 00:45:50,800
She has begun to speed up,

637
00:45:50,880 --> 00:45:52,880
easily increasing her distance

638
00:45:52,960 --> 00:45:54,200
from No. 308.

639
00:46:16,360 --> 00:46:18,720
JUNIOR WOMEN'S 3000 M LAP COUNT

640
00:46:18,800 --> 00:46:20,960
LI ZHENG

641
00:46:21,040 --> 00:46:25,680
- Go!
- Go!

642
00:46:25,760 --> 00:46:27,440
What's No. 308's major?

643
00:46:27,520 --> 00:46:31,160
She's a tough one to run
in those shoes. Her legs will fall off.

644
00:46:32,720 --> 00:46:35,160
You should be at the finish line
when 323 crosses.

645
00:46:35,240 --> 00:46:36,960
Already? I have to go.

646
00:46:40,480 --> 00:46:42,240
ZHENG YU

647
00:46:42,320 --> 00:46:43,160
- Go!
- Go!

648
00:46:43,240 --> 00:46:45,200
- Go!
- Go!

649
00:46:45,280 --> 00:46:46,120
I can't go on.

650
00:46:46,200 --> 00:46:47,280
Forget it.

651
00:46:47,360 --> 00:46:48,880
Let's go.

652
00:46:48,960 --> 00:46:51,280
LU JIAMEI

653
00:46:59,000 --> 00:47:01,320
LI ZHENG

654
00:47:02,680 --> 00:47:04,120
It's the last 100 m.

655
00:47:04,200 --> 00:47:07,160
No. 323 sprints across the finish line!

656
00:47:07,240 --> 00:47:09,680
Congratulations, No. 323!

657
00:47:16,840 --> 00:47:18,040
TONG RUYI

658
00:47:21,640 --> 00:47:22,480
- Go!
- Go!

659
00:47:22,560 --> 00:47:24,320
- Go!
- Go!

660
00:47:24,400 --> 00:47:27,680
- Go!
- Go!

661
00:47:27,760 --> 00:47:28,760
Final half lap.

662
00:47:28,840 --> 00:47:30,960
- Go!
- Go!

663
00:47:31,040 --> 00:47:35,280
- Go!
- Go!

664
00:47:35,360 --> 00:47:38,600
- Go!
- Go!

665
00:47:38,680 --> 00:47:42,560
- Go!
- Go!

666
00:47:42,640 --> 00:47:44,480
- Go!
- Go!

667
00:47:47,800 --> 00:47:49,880
- Is she okay?
- Right. Is something wrong?

668
00:47:55,800 --> 00:47:57,480
I'm here, Chen Yanzhou!

669
00:47:57,560 --> 00:47:58,400
Thanks so much!

670
00:47:59,000 --> 00:48:01,080
Still three runners left. Mark their laps.

671
00:48:54,320 --> 00:48:55,720
Why are you standing here?

672
00:48:55,800 --> 00:48:58,960
Sad that you failed the test,
so you're standing in the rain?

673
00:48:59,920 --> 00:49:01,800
No, I'm just looking.

674
00:49:03,120 --> 00:49:04,040
Looking at what?

675
00:49:04,960 --> 00:49:06,760
Looking for anyone like me,

676
00:49:06,840 --> 00:49:08,000
unsure of where to go.

677
00:49:11,280 --> 00:49:12,480
Have you found anyone?

678
00:49:15,880 --> 00:49:16,840
Yes.

679
00:49:21,440 --> 00:49:22,480
<i>How strange.</i>

680
00:49:23,280 --> 00:49:24,840
<i>We both lost.</i>

681
00:49:25,400 --> 00:49:28,560
<i>But I feel less lonely than when I win.</i>

682
00:49:29,880 --> 00:49:31,040
<i>It's not love.</i>

683
00:49:31,120 --> 00:49:32,680
<i>Nor is it friendship.</i>

684
00:49:33,320 --> 00:49:34,840
<i>It's not even understanding.</i>

685
00:49:36,080 --> 00:49:37,760
<i>It's just a confirmation of sorts.</i>

686
00:49:38,480 --> 00:49:40,440
<i>Confirmation that someone else</i>

687
00:49:40,520 --> 00:49:42,000
<i>is just like you,</i>

688
00:49:42,880 --> 00:49:43,920
<i>caught in the rain.</i>
